ut:\\n 29|     - list[int] of NEW candidate indices (no repeats; already-selected may be ignored/replaced by runner).\\n 30|     \\n 31|     Strategy: Thompson Sampling with Gene Cluster Priors\\n 32|     - Uses Thompson Sampling (Bayesian bandit algorithm) for adaptive exploration-exploitation\\n 33|     - Models each candidate with Beta distribution based on hit observations\\n 34|     - Uses gene search to create clusters and share information via Bayesian priors\\n 35|     - Enhanced fallback: Uses gene name prefix clustering when gene search unavailable\\n 36|     - Naturally balances exploration vs exploitation based on uncertainty\\n 37|     \\"\\"\\"\\n 38|     rng = random.Random(seed)\\n 39|     np.random.seed(seed)\\n 40|     \\n 41|     # Get already selected indices\\n 42|     selected = set(h[\'candidate_index\'] for h in history)\\n 43|     \\n 44|     # Get all available candidate indices\\n 45|     all_indices = list(range(len(candidates)))\\n 46|     available = [i for i in all_indices if i not in selected]\\n 47|     \\n 48|     if len(available) <= batch_size:\\n 49|         return available\\n 50|     \\n 51|     # If no history, use pure exploration\\n 52|     if len(history) == 0:\\n 53|         return rng.sample(available, batch_size)\\n 54|     \\n 55|     # Check if hit information is available\\n 56|     has_hits = any(\'hit\' in h for h in history)\\n 57|     \\n 58|     if not has_hits:\\n 59|         # Fall back to score-based selection using absolute scores\\n 60|         sorted_history = sorted(history, key=lambda x: abs(x[\'score\']), reverse=True)\\n 61|         top_k = max(10, len(sorted_history) // 5)\\n 62|         top_performers = [h[\'candidate_index\'] for h in sorted_history[:top_k]]\\n 63|         \\n 64|         # Sample from top performers\\n 65|         selected_indices = []\\n 66|         remaining = available.copy()\\n 67|         \\n 68|         # Take some top performers if available\\n 69|         top_available = [idx for idx in top_performers if idx in remaining]\\n 70|         if top_available:\\n 71|             n_top = min(len(top_available), batch_size // 2)\\n 72|             selected_indices.extend(rng.sample(top_available, n_top))\\n 73|             remaining = [i for i in remaining if i not in selected_indices]\\n 74|         \\n 75|         # Fill rest with random exploration\\n 76|         if len(selected_indices) < batch_size:\\n 77|             needed = batch_size - len(selected_indices)\\n 78|             selected_indices.extend(rng.sample(remaining, min(needed, len(remaining))))\\n 79|         \\n 80|         return selected_indices[:batch_size]\\n 81|     \\n 82|     # Enhanced Thompson Sampling with Continuous Score Modeling\\n 83|     # Use Gaussian-Gamma model for continuous scores instead of Beta for binary hits\\n 84|     \\n 85|     # Group candidates into clusters based on gene similarity\\n 86|     clusters = defaultdict(list)\\n 87|     candidate_to_cluster = {}\\n 88|     \\n 89|     # Try to use gene search to create clusters\\n 90|     try:\\n 91|         import bda_tools\\n 92|         \\n 93|         # Create clusters for all candidates we have history for\\n 94|         for h in history:\\n 95|             idx = h[\'candidate_index\']\\n 96|             candidate = candidates[idx]\\n 97|             gene = candidate.get(\'gene\') or candidate.get(\'gene_a\')\\n 98|             \\n 99|             if gene and idx not in candidate_to_cluster:\\n100|                 # Find similar genes\\n101|                 try:\\n102|                     similar = bda_tools.gene_search(gene, k=20, diverse=False)\\n103|                     cluster_id = f\\"cluster_{gene}\\"\\n104|                     \\n105|                     for sim_idx in similar:\\n106|                         if sim_idx not in candidate_to_cluster:\\n107|                             candidate_to_cluster[sim_idx] = cluster_id\\n108|                             clusters[cluster_id].append(sim_idx)\\n109|                 except:\\n110|                     # If gene search fails, put in singleton cluster\\n111|                     cluster_id = f\\"singleton_{idx}\\"\\n112|                     candidate_to_cluster[idx] = cluster_id\\n113|                     clusters[cluster_id] = [idx]\\n114|         \\n115|         # Assign unassigned candidates to singleton clusters\\n116|         for idx in all_indices:\\n117|             if idx not in candidate_to_cluster:\\n118|                 cluster_id = f\\"singleton_{idx}\\"\\n119|                 candidate_to_cluster[idx] = cluster_id\\n120|                 clusters[cluster_id] = [idx]\\n121|                 \\n122|     except ImportError:\\n123|         # No gene search available - use enhanced fallback: gene family prefix clustering\\n124|         # Group genes by name prefix to capture gene families (e.g., ZNF, ZSCAN, TNF, etc.)\\n125|         gene_to_prefix = {}\\n126|         \\n127|         for idx in all_indices:\\n128|             candidate = candidates[idx]\\n129|             gene = candidate.get(\'gene\') or candidate.get(\'gene_a\')\\n130|             if gene:\\n131|                 # Extract prefix: typically first 3-4 letters before numbers\\n132|                 # This captures gene families like ZNF, ZSCAN, TNF, IL, etc.\\n133|                 prefix = \'\'.join([c for c in gene if not c.isdigit()])[:4]\\n134|                 if len(prefix) >= 2:\\n135|                     gene_to_prefix[idx] = f\\"family_{prefix}\\"\\n136|                 else:\\n137|                     gene_to_prefix[idx] = f\\"singleton_{idx}\\"\\n138|             else:\\n139|                 gene_to_prefix[idx] = f\\"singleton_{idx}\\"\\n140|         \\n141|         # Create clusters based on prefix\\n142|         for idx, prefix in gene_to_prefix.items():\\n143|             candidate_to_cluster[idx] = prefix\\n144|             clusters[prefix].append(idx)\\n145|     \\n146|     # Compute cluster statistics using continuous scores\\n147|     cluster_sums = defaultdict(float)\\n148|     cluster_sums_sq = defaultdict(float)\\n149|     cluster_counts = defaultdict(int)\\n150|     \\n151|     for h in history:\\n152|         idx = h[\'candidate_index\']\\n153|         cluster_id = candidate_to_cluster[idx]\\n154|         score = h[\'score\']\\n155|         \\n156|         cluster_sums[cluster_id] += score\\n157|         cluster_sums_sq[cluster_id] += score * score\\n158|         cluster_counts[cluster_id] += 1\\n159|     \\n160|     # Compute global statistics for empirical Bayes prior\\n161|     all_scores = [h[\'score\'] for h in history]\\n162|     global_mean = np.mean(all_scores) if all_scores else 0.0\\n163|     global_var = np.var(all_scores) if len(all_scores) > 1 else 1.0\\n164|     \\n165|     # Gaussian-Gamma prior parameters (uninformative but centered at global stats)\\n166|     mu_0 = global_mean  # Prior mean\\n167|     lambda_0 = 1.0      # Prior precision scaling\\n168|     alpha_0 = 1.0       # Prior shape for precision\\n169|     beta_0 = global_var if global_var > 0 else 1.0  # Prior rate for precision\\n170|     \\n171|     # For each cluster, compute posterior parameters\\n172|     cluster_posterior = {}\\n173|     \\n174|     for cluster_id in clusters:\\n175|         n = cluster_counts.get(cluster_id, 0)\\n176|         \\n177|         if n == 0:\\n178|             # No observations, use prior\\n179|             cluster_posterior[cluster_id] = {\\n180|                 \'mu_n\': mu_0,\\n181|                 \'lambda_n\': lambda_0,\\n182|                 \'alpha_n\': alpha_0,\\n183|                 \'beta_n\': beta_0\\n184|             }\\n185|         else:\\n186|             # Update posterior with cluster observations\\n187|             sum_x = cluster_sums[cluster_id]\\n188|             sum_x_sq = cluster_sums_sq[cluster_id]\\n189|             mean_x = sum_x / n\\n190|             \\n191|             # Gaussian-Gamma posterior update\\n192|             lambda_n = lambda_0 + n\\n193|             mu_n = (lambda_0 * mu_0 + sum_x) / lambda_n\\n194|             alpha_n = alpha_0 + n / 2.0\\n195|             beta_n = beta_0 + 0.5 * (sum_x_sq - (sum_x * sum_x) / n) + \\\\\\n196|                      (lambda_0 * n * (mean_x - mu_0) ** 2) / (2 * lambda_n)\\n197|             \\n198|             cluster_posterior[cluster_id] = {\\n199|                 \'mu_n\': mu_n,\\n200|                 \'lambda_n\': lambda_n,\\n201|                 \'alpha_n\': alpha_n,\\n202|                 \'beta_n\': beta_n\\n203|             }\\n204|     \\n205|     # For candidates with direct observations, compute posterior\\n206|     candidate_posterior = {}\\n207|     \\n208|     for h in history:\\n209|         idx = h[\'candidate_index\']\\n210|         score = h[\'score\']\\n211|         cluster_id = candidate_to_cluster[idx]\\n212|         cluster_post = cluster_posterior[cluster_id]\\n213|         \\n214|         # Conservative update: treat cluster prior as having stronger weight\\n215|         # This prevents overfitting to a single observation when cluster has limited data\\n216|         effective_prior_weight = max(cluster_post[\'lambda_n\'], 2.0)  # At least 2 pseudo-observations\\n217|         lambda_n = effective_prior_weight + 1\\n218|         mu_n = (effective_prior_weight * cluster_post[\'mu_n\'] + score) / lambda_n\\n219|         alpha_n = cluster_post[\'alpha_n\'] + 0.5\\n220|         beta_n = cluster_post[\'beta_n\'] + 0.5 * (score - cluster_post[\'mu_n\']) ** 2 * \\\\\\n221|                  effective_prior_weight / lambda_n\\n222|         \\n223|         candidate_posterior[idx] = {\\n224|             \'mu_n\': mu_n,\\n225|             \'lambda_n\': lambda_n,\\n226|             \'alpha_n\': alpha_n,\\n227|             \'beta_n\': beta_n\\n228|         }\\n229|     \\n230|     # Thompson Sampling: sample from posterior predictive (Student-t)\\n231|     sampled_scores = {}\\n232|     \\n233|     for idx in available:\\n234|         cluster_id = candidate_to_cluster[idx]\\n235|         \\n236|         if idx in candidate_posterior:\\n237|             # Candidate has been observed, use its posterior\\n238|             post = candidate_posterior[idx]\\n239|         else:\\n240|             # Candidate not observed, use cluster posterior\\n241|             post = cluster_posterior[cluster_id]\\n242|         \\n243|         # Sample precision from Gamma\\n244|         tau = np.random.gamma(post[\'alpha_n\'], 1.0 / post[\'beta_n\'])\\n245|         \\n246|         # Sample mean from Gaussian given precision\\n247|         mean_sample = np.random.normal(post[\'mu_n\'], 1.0 / np.sqrt(post[\'lambda_n\'] * tau))\\n248|         \\n249|         # Store sampled score (we want more negative = better for this task)\\n250|         sampled_scores[idx] = mean_sample\\n251|     \\n252|     # Select top candidates by sampled score (prioritize more negative values)\\n253|     sorted_by_sample = sorted(available, key=lambda x: sampled_scores[x])\\n254|     selected_indices = sorted_by_sample[:batch_size]\\n255|     \\n256|     return selected_indices"\n}'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Now let me check the harness run script to understand the execution environment:\n', 'tool_calls': [{'id': 'call_a92c805326ce4ebe9a43aff5', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'read_file', 'arguments': '{"file_path": "/inspire/qb-ilm/project/cq-scientific-cooperation-zone/public/ywang/meta-harness-evolver/project/test/project-bda/harness_run_script.sh"}'}}]}, {'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_a92c805326ce4ebe9a43aff5', 'content': '{\n  "content": " 1| #!/usr/bin/env bash\\n 2| set -euo pipefail\\n 3| \\n 4| # Usage: bash harness_run_script.sh <candidate_dir>\\n 5| CANDIDATE_DIR=\\"${1:-${CANDIDATE_DIR:-}}\\"\\n 6| if [[ -z \\"$CANDIDATE_DIR\\" ]]; then\\n 7|   echo \\"Usage: bash harness_run_script.sh <candidate_dir>\\" >&2\\n 8|   exit 2\\n 9| fi\\n10| \\n11| CANDIDATE_DIR=\\"$(cd \\"$CANDIDATE_DIR\\" && pwd)\\"\\n12| HARNESS_DIR=\\"$CANDIDATE_DIR/harness\\"\\n13| PROJECT_DIR=\\"$(cd \\"$(dirname \\"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\\")\\" && pwd)\\"\\n14| PROJECT_MAIN=\\"$PROJECT_DIR/main_fix_train_test_input_output.py\\"\\n15| \\n16| if [[ ! -d \\"$HARNESS_DIR\\" ]]; then\\n17|   echo \\"Missing harness dir: $HARNESS_DIR\\" >&2\\n18|   exit 2\\n19| fi\\n20| if [[ ! -f \\"$PROJECT_MAIN\\" ]]; then\\n21|   echo \\"Missing main file: $PROJECT_MAIN\\" >&2\\n22|   exit 2\\n23| fi\\n24| \\n25| # 数据/运行时配置（需要时可通过环境变量覆盖）。\\n26| # 迁移到其它机器时需要检查：\\n27| # - PYTHON_BIN 是否指向目标机器上的正确 Python/conda 环境。\\n28| # - BDA_DATASETS_DIR 必须指向本地 BDA 数据集目录。\\n29| # - BDA_STATE_PATH 是可选项；如果运行需要跨机器恢复，需要设置为\\n30| #   可写且可恢复的状态文件路径。\\n31| PYTHON_BIN=\\"${PYTHON_BIN:-python}\\"\\n32| MODEL_IMPL_PATH=\\"$HARNESS_DIR/model.py\\"\\n33| if [[ ! -f \\"$MODEL_IMPL_PATH\\" ]]; then\\n34|   echo \\"Model file not found: $MODEL_IMPL_PATH\\" >&2\\n35|   exit 2\\n36| fi\\n37| \\n38| BDA_DATA_NAME=\\"${BDA_DATA_NAME:-IFNG}\\"\\n39| BDA_TASK=\\"${BDA_TASK:-perturb-genes-brief}\\"\\n40| BDA_STEPS=\\"${BDA_STEPS:-5}\\"\\n41| BDA_NUM_GENES=\\"${BDA_NUM_GENES:-128}\\"\\n42| BDA_SEED=\\"${BDA_SEED:-42}\\"\\n43| BDA_RESUME_STATE=\\"${BDA_RESUME_STATE:-1}\\"\\n44| BDA_INCLUDE_HIT_IN_HISTORY=\\"${BDA_INCLUDE_HIT_IN_HISTORY:-1}\\"\\n45| \\n46| BDA_WORKSPACE_DIR=\\"${EVOLVER_WORKSPACE:-}\\"\\n47| if [[ -z \\"$BDA_WORKSPACE_DIR\\" ]]; then\\n48|   BDA_WORKSPACE_DIR=\\"$(cd \\"$CANDIDATE_DIR/../..\\" && pwd)\\"\\n49| fi\\n50| if [[ -z \\"${BDA_STATE_PATH:-}\\" ]]; then\\n51|   export BDA_STATE_PATH=\\"$BDA_WORKSPACE_DIR/bda_state.json\\"\\n52| fi\\n53| \\n54| if [[ -z \\"${BDA_DATASETS_DIR:-}\\" ]]; then\\n55|   echo \\"BDA_DATASETS_DIR is required; set it to the BioDiscoveryAgent datasets directory.\\" >&2\\n56|   exit 2\\n57| fi\\n58| if [[ ! -d \\"$BDA_DATASETS_DIR\\" ]]; then\\n59|   echo \\"BDA_DATASETS_DIR does not exist or is not a directory: $BDA_DATASETS_DIR\\" >&2\\n60|   exit 2\\n61| fi\\n62| \\n63| ARGS=(\\n64|   \\"$PYTHON_BIN\\" \\"$PROJECT_MAIN\\"\\n65|   --mode bda_active_search\\n66|   --data_name \\"$BDA_DATA_NAME\\"\\n67|   --task \\"$BDA_TASK\\"\\n68|   --steps \\"$BDA_STEPS\\"\\n69|   --batch_size \\"$BDA_NUM_GENES\\"\\n70|   --seed \\"$BDA_SEED\\"\\n71|   --model_dir \\"$MODEL_IMPL_PATH\\"\\n72|   --resume_state \\"$BDA_RESUME_STATE\\"\\n73|   --include_hit_in_history \\"$BDA_INCLUDE_HIT_IN_HISTORY\\"\\n74|   --datasets_dir \\"$BDA_DATASETS_DIR\\"\\n75| )\\n76| if [[ -n \\"${BDA_STATE_PATH:-}\\" ]]; then\\n77|   ARGS+=(--state_path \\"$BDA_STATE_PATH\\")\\n78| fi\\n79| \\n80| \\"${ARGS[@]}\\""\n}'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Now let me analyze the evolution patterns:\n\n## Analysis Summary\n\n**Score Progression:**\n- Candidate 1: 16.83 (5 hits in 128 queries)\n- Candidate 2: 20.32 (10 hits in 256 queries) - Improved by using continuous scores\n- Candidate 3: 22.35 (16 hits in 384 queries) - Best score with conservative update\n\n**Key Changes:**\n1. **Candidate 1 → 2**: Switched from Beta distribution (binary hits) to Gaussian-Gamma (continuous scores)\n2. **Candidate 2 → 3**: Added conservative update with `effective_prior_weight = max(cluster_post['lambda_n'], 2.0)` to prevent overfitting\n\n**Current Model (Candidate 3):**\n- Uses Gaussian-Gamma Bayesian model for continuous scores\n- Conservative Bayesian update (effective_prior_weight ensures minimum of 2 pseudo-observations)\n- Gene clustering via bda_tools or prefix-based fallback\n- Thompson Sampling for exploration-exploitation\n\n**Hypothesis:**\nThe conservative update in candidate 3 is working well, but we might be able to improve it further by making the exploration more targeted. Looking at the metrics, the hit rate improved from 5→10→16 hits across rounds. The task is to find genes that decrease tau protein (more negative scores are better).\n\nLet me check the metrics more carefully to see what patterns emerge:\n", 'tool_calls': [{'id': 'call_a49b0389c35c4cf0a0082192', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'read_file', 'a